## User override

There is no standing bypass and no marker file. The user may lift ADP
enforcement only per action, by stating explicit authorization for that one
specific action in their own prompt text (for example, "I explicitly
authorize this action"). That authorization allows exactly the one
otherwise-blocked decision it names and is then consumed; it does not carry
forward, including to an identical repeat of the same tool call. Workers
relay a user's authorization request to the parent rather than acting on
their own inference; never infer authorization from a blocked operation.
Host permissions and other protocols remain in force regardless.
